WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:02.770
Hello, I'm Brian Poole.

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.490
I'm the Technical Program Manager at Epic Games,

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.210
and I'm here to talk to you today about camera configuration

4
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.570
for ICDFX.

5
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.609
Let's take a look at our slide deck here and our training

6
00:00:13.609 --> 00:00:14.490
outline.

7
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.010
So we're going to go over hardware configuration, where

8
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.010
we'll talk about camera choices, sensor types

9
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.530
and sizes, Unreal film back settings,

10
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.969
building your own camera rig, and how we connect

11
00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:28.170
the camera to the system.

12
00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:32.609
Then we'll move in and talk about SDI and timecode and genlock.

13
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:34.369
We'll give you a simplified wiring

14
00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:38.090
diagram of what a typical ICDFX studio looks like.

15
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.250
We'll talk about the various ports on the camera,

16
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.289
the SDI connections, and all the various precautions

17
00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:46.090
you need to take when hooking up your camera gear.

18
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.929
We'll talk about timecode, the different types

19
00:00:48.929 --> 00:00:52.450
and configurations, a little bit on how to jam timecode

20
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.250
into your camera if your camera has a particular issue.

21
00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.570
We'll also go over genlock types and configuration

22
00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.929
and talk about latency issues that you

23
00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:07.489
might encounter when working on your ICDFX stage.

24
00:01:07.489 --> 00:01:11.010
Then we'll have a section on media profiles,

25
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.370
in which you will learn about the setup of creating

26
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.650
a media profile in Unreal Engine.

27
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.969
And then finally, we'll have a portion

28
00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:21.890
on ICDFX cinematography techniques,

29
00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.129
where we'll talk about virtual production guidelines,

30
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.010
visual acuity, how to counter flicker, frame rate

31
00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.650
and refresh issues, and a little bit

32
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.650
on shutter, shutter angle, shutter speed,

33
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:39.090
and how to handle Moir and Moir mitigation.

34
00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.489
That concludes the training outline for today.

35
00:01:41.489 --> 00:01:44.530
Let's get into hardware configuration.
